{{also|Muffin}}
==English==
[[File:Mmm...English_muffins_(5393409247).jpg|right|thumb|A muffin (sense 1, an [[English muffin]]).]]
[[File:Muffin_NIH.jpg|right|thumb|A muffin (sense 2) with a spreading [[muffin top]].]]

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|en|moofin}}, of uncertain origin. Possibly from {{bor|en|nds|muffen}}, plural of {{m|nds|muffe|t=small cake}}, or perhaps a diminutive of {{m|nds|muffe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmʌfɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-muffin.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌfɪn}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|British}} A type of [[flattish]] bun, usually cut in two [[horizontally]], [[toast]]ed and spread with butter, etc, before being eaten; an [[English muffin]].
# A [[cupcake]]-shaped baked good (for example of [[cornbread]], [[banana bread]], or a chocolate dough), sometimes glazed but typically without frosting, eaten especially for breakfast (in contrast to a cupcake, which is a [[dessert]]).
#* {{seeCites|en}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[mechanism]] used in the [[w:Java Network Launching Protocol|Java Network Launching Protocol]] [[analogous]] to the [[cookie]] mechanism and which permits a program running in a [[browser]] to perform operations on a client machine.
#* '''2001''', ''JNLP and Java Web Start'', Sun Developer Network, Technical Articles and Tips, 30 May 2001:
#*: The name/value pairs provided by the PersistenceService are similar to browser cookies. The Java Web Start implementation honors this legacy by naming the pairs "'''muffins'''.
# {{lb|en|slang}} {{non-gloss definition|Term of endearment.}}<!--, e.g. "nuffin' muffin"-->
#: ''I love you, '''muffin'''!''
# {{lb|en|sexual slang}} A [[vulva]].
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1986|artist={{w|Mojo Nixon}} and {{w|Skid Roper}}|title=Stuffin' Martha's Muffin|album={{w|Frenzy (Mojo Nixon album)|Frenzy}}|passage=I wanna be stuffin' {{w|Martha Quinn|Martha's}} '''muffin'''!}}
# {{lb|en|baseball|slang}} A less [[talented]] player; one who [[muff]]s, or drops the ball.
# {{lb|en|slang}} A charming, attractive young man. <!--Ch1908: "one who dangles after a young woman"--> {{rfex|en}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[small]] [[plate]], smaller than a [[twiffler]]. <!--Chambers 1908-->

